    "result_text": "The only tests are the 11 acceptance checkpoint classes, and all 21 tests pass with `BUILD SUCCESS`.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the **shares-household / householdId** feature (checkpoint Cp11) for the Spring Boot PetClinic REST app.\n\nThe Cp10 logic (rejecting same-lastName + same-address, and allowing it when `sharesHousehold == true`) was already present. Cp11 additionally requires assigning and returning a stable shared `householdId`.\n\n**Changes:**\n\n1. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 Added a read-only `householdId` string property to the `Owner` response schema (generates the DTO getter/setter, auto-mapped by MapStruct since the name matches the model field).\n\n2. **`model/Owner.java`** \u2014 Added a `householdId` field with `@Column(name = \"household_id\")` plus getter/setter.\n\n3. **`db/{hsqldb,h2,postgres,mysql}/schema.sql`** \u2014 Added the `household_id` column to the `owners` table for every DB variant (tests run on hsqldb).\n\n4. **`rest/controller/v1/OwnerRestControllerV1.java`** \u2014 Added `assignHouseholdId(owner)` in `addOwner`, deriving the id deterministically as `HH-<first 12 upper-hex chars of SHA-256(collapse(lastName) + \"\\n\" + collapse(address))>`, using the same `collapse()` canonicalization (trim, collapse whitespace, lower-case) the household-duplicate check uses.\n\n**Why deterministic-from-fields:** Because the id is derived purely from the canonicalized lastName + address, every owner in the same household gets the *same* value regardless of creation order \u2014 the pre-existing owner and each `sharesHousehold` joiner all match. This satisfies \"a stable shared identifier\" robustly without needing to look up and copy an existing member's id.\n\nResult: full suite green \u2014 **21 tests run, 0 failures, 0 errors, BUILD SUCCESS** (including `Cp11Tests.coreJoinersShareHouseholdId` and the three `Cp10Tests`).",
